WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:04.280
Karen was one of the
kindest, sweetest people.

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:05.580
I was able to sit down with her

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.920
and her husband Tom in-person,

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.700
and just get to know them a little bit.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.640
I remember her talking
about her favorite color.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:14.620
She was wearing purple.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.280
She had a purple bracelet
on, purple sunglasses.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.580
She was really excited
about the possibility

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.130
of her and Tom being retired recently

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.940
and being able to do things,

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.310
but I think the reality
was sort of setting in that

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:30.170
some of that travel she had thought about

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:33.350
might not be happening
because she was too sick.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:37.010
Basically a pretty healthy
70 something year old woman

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.980
surprised to be diagnosed
with liver cancer.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.490
That was very aggressive.

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:45.440
Her doctors were surprised too.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.900
When she received the recall
notice from her pharmacy

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.270
she started to put pieces together.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.220
If you are taking heart medication

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:56.710
as so many Canadians are,

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.200
you may wanna double check
your label this morning.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.140
The FDA has expanded the list of drugs

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:04.823
being recalled that contain valsartan.

00:01:04.823 --> 00:01:07.050
A drug recall over cancer concerns

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.700
as many patients confused.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.040
Researchers have linked that
chemical to several cancers.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:15.500
22 other countries have also
already recalled the drug

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.820
for the very same reasons.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:21.030
Karen had been taking valsartan

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.600
possibly for as long as four years,

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.480
she ended up dying recently from cancer.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.290
They're testing 100% of the drugs

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:30.440
that come into this country,

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.530
is that how it works to keep me safe?

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.430
No, and I think a lot of
people assume that for sure.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:38.240
Everyone is pushing for cheaper drugs.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.930
And what this one example shows is that

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:43.610
safety is one of the costs.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.116
And we don't even know that
we're being asked to pay it.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:55.340
My name is Anna Edney.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.060
I'm a health policy
reporter at Bloomberg News.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:02.360
I wrote the article titled
Tainted Pills, Broken Trust

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.100
with Susan Berfield,

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:06.493
who is also a colleague
of mine at Bloomberg.

00:02:08.242 --> 00:02:13.240
Valsartan was a drug and it's
used to lower blood pressure

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:15.820
which is something many,
many Americans use.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:19.070
I mean, the pills they were
used by millions of people.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:22.370
It was found that the drug
had carcinogens in it.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.780
I had followed issues with drug quality

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.330
for a really long time.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:29.703
And this was sort of one of
the worst ones that I had seen.

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:38.040
The chemical that had been
found in the valsartan

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.970
the shorthand is NDMA.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:43.000
It's a chemical that used to be used

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.980
in rocket fuel production

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:49.223
and is also now created
through industrial processes.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.640
It is created when food is smoked.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.620
So that's why there's some concern

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.110
about eating too much bacon.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:02.430
NDMA is also the reason that
secondhand smoke is a problem.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:06.133
It's a probable carcinogen
that's created in many ways.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.250
People who had been
taking valsartan regularly

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:11.510
as most people do,

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:14.930
there was a concern that
there could be some connection

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:17.540
to cancer of the liver,

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:20.020
in particular we knew the end result

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.500
was a contaminated medicine.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.763
And then we began looking backward.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:30.060
When a company files an
application for a new drug

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.060
to the Food and Drug Administration,

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:35.160
they've done very large clinical trials

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:38.620
looking at the efficacy
and the safety of a drug.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:41.460
And these have lasted months if not years.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:43.390
Generics are different though.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:48.020
Generics are the drugs
that have gone off patent.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.380
The company that did the
research into the drug

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:52.370
gets a certain 10, 20 year period

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.930
where they are the only
ones who can sell it.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:56.280
Then after that other companies can make

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.953
essentially copies of the drug.

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.520
What they have to show the FDA

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.160
is just that they work in the same way.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.780
So they're not really doing
these large clinical trials.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.910
They're saying we took your formula

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:12.300
and we think ours works exactly the same.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.150
So it should be fine.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.850
Generics are much cheaper

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:19.840
because they don't have to
bear the research costs.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:22.370
So it become hugely popular.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:26.220
Almost 90% of the drugs
that everyone in America

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.103
is prescribed are generics.

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:31.780
The valsartan is the generic form

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:34.110
of a drug that Novartis created.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.580
It was enormous success for Novartis.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.240
Billions and billions of dollars,

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.563
among the most popular
drugs on the planet.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:45.570
When it went off patent,
there were a lot of companies

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:48.993
that were rushing to create
generic versions of them.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.980
Over the past years,

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:55.380
more and more are being
manufactured overseas.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.720
That is largely a financial decision.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:03.590
As we know now, labor
and and often supplies

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.240
can be cheaper overseas.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:09.940
There has been so much
pressure on the medical system

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.220
to approve drugs that
can be made more cheaply

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:15.670
and then to have them sold more cheaply

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.783
to American consumers.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:22.710
The FDA tests probably
less than 1% of the supply

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.810
that comes into the US every year.

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:26.390
And many of our drugs are coming

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:29.220
from particularly China and India.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.680
And so not much of it at all gets tested.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:36.110
It's a huge industry and
the FDA is not all that big

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:37.850
and not all that well-funded.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:40.920
And so they ask that the industry

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.940
keeps up with quality testing

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.530
that essentially it's up to them,

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:47.910
because they're the ones
with their names on the line.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:51.730
In China and India, the FDA
has found a lot of issues

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:53.770
with quality control.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:55.770
Generics don't bring in a lot of money.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:59.530
So any ability to save
something here and there

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:02.070
with the type of ingredient
that you might use,

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:05.260
or the process you might use,
the incentive is much higher.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.290
And so the quality can suffer sometimes

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:10.683
when money becomes the bottom line.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:18.200
Zhejiang Huahai was
manufacturer of what's called

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:21.020
the active ingredient in the valsartan.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.940
So they need essentially
the part of the drug

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.400
that has the effect,

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.840
and then they would sell
it to other manufacturers

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:32.360
who would kind of finish it
with inactive ingredients

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.770
and the coding that you see
so that you can take it.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:37.830
Huahai was founded in 1989

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:41.220
and has been committed to
supplying high quality medicine,

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:43.570
active pharmaceutical ingredients,

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:46.990
and advanced intermediates
for our customers.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:51.700
Huahai decided to use a
solvent that was cheaper

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.683
than the one Novartis had been using.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:58.873
They wanted to save
money however they could.

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:02.890
They changed it to a
solvent that's called DMF.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.250
When Huahai changed the solvent

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:07.920
it said that it wasn't a huge change

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.950
and it landed the FDA but it said

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:12.870
that it wasn't a critical change.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.950
Just that rephrasing was very important

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:19.430
because it would invite less scrutiny

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:23.850
and suggested that it was
a pretty ordinary change

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:26.400
that was done for reasons

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.190
that were really very
crucial to the process.

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:32.950
And both of those things proved untrue.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.230
It was critical because
the ingredients in it

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:40.230
reacted with ingredients in
valsartan to form the NDMA.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:49.290
One of the hardest parts
with reporting the story

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:54.290
is that the FDA inspection
process is very secretive.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:59.510
So it can be difficult
to get the documents.

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:02.180
Once you do get them through the FDA,

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:03.803
they're heavily redacted.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:07.550
What we found in particular
with Huahai is that

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.040
there had been inspections.

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:11.800
And the inspectors had found problems

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.430
like rusty and old machinery,

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.370
but more important than
that discovered that

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:20.660
Huahai had found impurities,

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:23.660
essentially kind of in their testing.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.750
When a company does quality testing,

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:28.710
some of the readouts
sort of look like an EKG,

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:31.730
like a heart rhythm, they're
waves going up and down

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:33.700
that are indicating what's in the drug.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:37.160
And so the inspector found these peaks

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:38.960
that weren't supposed to be there.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:42.400
The management at Huahai
called them ghost peaks,

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.630
and he indicated that he
never heard of that before.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:47.080
He didn't know what that meant.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.250
And later it was found
out that that ghost peak,

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:55.010
what was indicating there
was NDMA in the drug.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.730
The inspector was worried enough

00:08:57.730 --> 00:09:01.100
that he recommended the FDA issue

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.840
what's called a warning letter.

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:05.930
And that is the most extreme
measure that the FDA can take.

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:09.480
And it essentially says
putting company on notice.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:13.410
The FDA decided not to do
that when it came to Huahai.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:17.200
And again, they said, we've
noticed this problems,

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:20.760
we'd like you to fix them
and report back to us.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.930
And essentially nothing
was done at that point.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:27.223
So Huahai did not move
immediately on the issue.

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:40.010
Novartis ordered valsartan
active ingredient

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.630
from Huahai in 2018.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:45.660
The company that had
originally made the brand name

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:49.200
blood pressure medication
was also making generics

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:54.200
and had bought 45 metric tons
of the active ingredient.

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:58.790
It arrived in Switzerland and
they began what we understand

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:01.200
to be routine testing of it.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:05.363
And discovered some
impurities, these peaks.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.450
This peak that Huahai
had seen, but ignored,

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:11.640
and Novartis that didn't look right.

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:14.890
And so they ended up trying to identify it

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:18.480
and they were able to
identify that it was NDMA.

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:21.320
Novartis notified Huahai of the problem.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:25.700
They notified the European
drug regulators and the FDA.

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:29.130
They began recalling the valsartan

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:31.670
that was produced by Huahai.

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:35.940
At the same time, they started
to test other suppliers

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.240
and began discovering
that the problem existed

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.580
beyond just Huahai.

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:43.420
The FDA has expanded its recall

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:47.190
of a common blood pressure
medicine due to cancer concerns.

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:49.120
Potentially millions of prescriptions

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:52.520
could be affected by this wide recall.

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:56.893
The recall began in the summer of 2018.

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:02.320
As we closed the story, the end of 2019,

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:05.510
there had been 52 separate recalls.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:08.480
And that's because the
testing was ongoing.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:11.090
The recalls continue for other drugs

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:12.930
that have NDMA in them.

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:16.340
And that's something I think
that is not going away.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:20.080
The FDA ultimately developed its own test.

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:24.950
The FDA issued a warning letter to Huahai.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:29.750
At the same time are trying
to allay consumer's concerns

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:33.320
about the risk of developing cancer.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:36.880
Repeating that though the levels of NDMA

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.210
in the valsartan were high,

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:42.530
they weren't really high
enough to be concerned.

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:45.510
They said like everyone
should not be checking

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:46.890
to see if they have cancer.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:49.300
And yet there are many,
many, many lawsuits

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.780
that are now in the courts
for that exact reason.

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:56.000
We know there was this problem.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.500
We know there are these people

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.330
who took the drug who are sick.

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:01.670
How closely we can make those connections

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:05.330
is something that probably
will need to be answered

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:09.093
both by medical experts and
in the courts at this point.

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.350
Millions of people took these drugs.

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:15.633
The impact I think, will
be seen for a long time.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:21.823
Safety concerns obviously
there, but they came second.

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:28.160
To a lot of people that
we spoke to they said,

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:32.620
well valsartan and the
NDMA that we found in it,

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:36.520
that's probably just one example.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.550
It's a terrible example because
it's a probable carcinogen,

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:44.340
but it's probably not the
only drug that's contaminated

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:45.560
or that will be contaminated,

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:48.550
because the system has vulnerabilities.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:53.550
Those vulnerabilities
will likely be exploited.

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:57.700
And you know, the
consequences will be borne

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:00.570
by the people who have the least say

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:01.920
in how any of this happens.

